  "summary": "Pompadours, pegged jeans and upright bass slaps: the 1950s that never left.",
  "description": "Rockabilly revival keeps 1950s Americana alive as living subculture: pompadour and duck-tail hair with actual pomade, cuffed selvedge denim, leather motorcycle jackets, swing dresses and victory rolls, the era's cars as totems, and its music lineage from Stray Cats (1979-) through psychobilly's horror-punk mutation (The Meteors, Nekromantix) to Japan's dedicated scene (Tokyo's Harajuku rockabillies since the 1980s). The culture is craft-heavy — pomade rituals, vintage sourcing, car-kustom kulture (pinstriping, lead sleds) — and visually cohesive enough to read instantly: the 1950s as defiant nostalgia with a danger curve.",
  "culturalContext": "Rockabilly revival keeps the 1950s a living subculture: Stray Cats to psychobilly to Tokyo's Harajuku scene, the culture sustains barber craft, vintage sourcing and kustom car kulture — the 1950s as defiant, dangerous nostalgia with pomade gloss.",
